.TH CBCBAYESMCMC2POS "1" "January 2026" "LALInference" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cbcBayesMCMC2pos \- Compute the evidence for a set of parallel tempered MCMC chains
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cbcBayesMCMC2pos.py
[\fI\,options\/\fR] \fI\,PTMCMC_datafile.hdf5 \/\fR[\fI\,PTMCMC_datafile2.hdf5 \/\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Compute the evidence for a set of parallel tempered MCMC chains
thourgh thermodynamical integration. If using several input PTMCMC files,
combine them into one set of posterior samples, weighted by their relative
evidences.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
show this help message and exit
.TP
\fB\-p\fR posterior.hdf5, \fB\-\-pos\fR=\fI\,posterior\/\fR.hdf5
Output file for posterior samples
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print some additional information
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-data\fR
datafile
.TP
\fB\-s\fR DOWNSAMPLE, \fB\-\-downsample\fR=\fI\,DOWNSAMPLE\/\fR
Approximate number of samples to record in the
posterior
.TP
\fB\-l\fR DELTALOGP, \fB\-\-deltaLogP\fR=\fI\,DELTALOGP\/\fR
Difference in logPosterior to use for convergence
test.
.TP
\fB\-b\fR, \fB\-\-fixedBurnin\fR
Fixed number of iteration for burnin.
.TP
\fB\-\-equal\-weighting\fR
Disable evidence weighting and just combine chains so
they have equal                        contribution to
the final result
.TP
\fB\-\-combine\-only\fR
Don't weight the chains at all, just concatenate them
(different length                        inputs will
have different representation in the output)
